      {
        "id": "overheating-is-the-engine-s-heart-attack",
        "title": "Overheating is the engine's heart attack",
        "description": "Engine overheating is the single most destructive thing that can happen to your engine. When your engine overheats, metal components expand beyond their design limits. Cylinder heads warp. Head gaskets fail. Pistons seize in cylinders. Blocks crack.",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "In our 24,650 quote dataset, we identified five primary causes of overheating:"
          },
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "level": "h4",
            "id": "",
            "text": "Coolant loss - 40% of cases"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "External leak or head gasket. Repair: £150-£2,000+."
          },
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "level": "h4",
            "id": "",
            "text": "Thermostat failure - 25% of cases"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Stuck closed, no coolant circulation. Repair: £80-£300."
          },
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "level": "h4",
            "id": "",
            "text": "Water pump failure - 20% of cases"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Pump impeller broken or leaking. Repair: £150-£700."
          },
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "level": "h4",
            "id": "",
            "text": "Radiator blockage - 10% of cases"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Blocked or damaged radiator. Repair: £300-£800."
          },
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "level": "h4",
            "id": "",
            "text": "Air in system - 5% of cases"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Low coolant or bleeding issue. Repair: £50-£150."
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "The critical rule: If your temperature gauge enters the red zone, you have seconds to minutes to stop the engine. Every second of overheating causes more damage."
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "The overheating escalation - cost progression"
          }
        ],
        "links": [],
        "source": {
          "sectionId": "overheating-is-the-engine-s-heart-attack",
          "order": 1
        }
      },
