      {
        "id": "the-expensive-mistake-is-thinking-you-can-make-it-home",
        "title": "The expensive mistake is thinking you can make it home",
        "description": "“The gauge is in the red, but I'm nearly there - I'll keep going.”",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "The 30 seconds you save could cost you £10,000. Stop immediately."
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "“I'll open the bonnet and add coolant while it's hot.”"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Never open the coolant reservoir when hot. Pressurised coolant will spray out and cause severe burns."
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "“The fan will save it - I'll just rev it.”"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Revving a hot engine increases temperature. Stop the engine immediately."
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "“Overheating is normal on a hot day.”"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "No. Your car's cooling system is designed for any UK weather. Overheating means something is broken."
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "“I'll just use water - it's fine.”"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Water isn't a substitute for coolant. It boils at a lower temperature and lacks corrosion inhibitors."
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "“The engine will be fine after it cools down.”"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "The damage is already done. Overheating causes warping and gasket failure even if it seems fine afterwards."
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Diagnostic flowchart"
          }
        ],
        "links": [],
        "source": {
          "sectionId": "the-expensive-mistake-is-thinking-you-can-make-it-home",
          "order": 4
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "follow-this-decision-tree-to-identify-the-cause",
        "title": "Follow this decision tree to identify the cause",
        "description": "ENGINE OVERHEATING │ ├─── Temperature gauge in red? │ │ │ ├── YES → STOP ENGINE IMMEDIATELY → Emergency │ │ │ └── NO → Rising but not red → Monitor closely │ ├─── Steam visible? │ │ │ ├── YES → Immediate stop → DO NOT DRIVE │ │ │ └── NO → Check coolant (when cold) │ ├─── Check coolant level (engine COLD) │ │ │ ├── Low → External leak → Coolant leak │ │ │ └── Normal → Thermostat or pump → Cooling system │ ├─── White smoke from exhaust? │ │ │ ├── YES → Head gasket → Head gasket │ │ │ └── NO → Check oil for mayo │ └─── Mayo in oil? │ ├── YES → Head gasket → Head gasket │ └── NO → Cooling system component → Cooling system",
