      {
        "id": "every-second-of-overheating-causes-more-damage",
        "title": "Every second of overheating causes more damage",
        "description": null,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "table",
            "headers": [
              "Time",
              "What Happens",
              "Temperature",
              "Cost"
            ],
            "rows": [
              [
                "Seconds",
                "Temperature enters red zone. Coolant boils. System pressure exceeds cap limit.",
                "120°C+",
                "£0 (stop now)"
              ],
              [
                "30 seconds",
                "Localised hot spots form. Cylinder head begins to warp. Head gasket starts to fail.",
                "130°C+",
                "£550-£2,000"
              ],
              [
                "1 minute",
                "Head gasket fails completely. Coolant enters combustion chambers and oil.",
                "140°C+",
                "£550-£2,000"
              ],
              [
                "2-3 minutes",
                "Cylinder head warps significantly. Pistons expand in cylinders.",
                "150°C+",
                "£1,000-£3,000"
              ],
              [
                "5 minutes",
                "Pistons seize in cylinders. Engine stops. Block may crack.",
                "160°C+",
                "£2,500-£10,000+"
              ]
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "The real-world rule: If your temperature gauge is in the red for more than 30 seconds, you've likely caused permanent damage."
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "What to do next"
          }
