      {
        "id": "stop-cool-inspect-diagnose",
        "title": "Stop, cool, inspect, diagnose",
        "description": null,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "list",
            "ordered": false,
            "items": [
              "Step 1: Stop driving (immediately) Pull over safely · Turn off engine · Wait 30+ minutes",
              "Step 2: Check coolant level (when cold) Wait at least 30 minutes · Open the coolant reservoir slowly (cover with a cloth) · Check level - is it below minimum?",
              "Step 3: Check for visible leaks Look for puddles under the car · Check hoses and radiator for damage · Look for dried coolant (white residue)",
              "Step 4: Check oil (dipstick/oil filler cap) Look for creamy/milky substance (mayonnaise) - this confirms coolant in oil = head gasket failure",
              "Step 5: Professional diagnostic (£50-£150) A technician will perform a cooling system pressure test, check for exhaust gases in coolant, inspect thermostat and water pump, and check radiator for blockage."
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Book Diagnostic"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Should you repair or replace?"
